   "question": "<h3><span style=\"color:#000000\">Two point charges repel each other with a force of 100 N. One of the charges is increased by 10% and the other is reduced by 10%. The new force of repulsion at the same distance would be</h3><h3>(A)<span style=\"color:#000000\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\">100 N<br />(B)<span style=\"color:#000000\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\">121 N<span style=\"color:#000000\"><br />(C)<span style=\"color:#000000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">99 N<br />(D)</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">None of these</span></span></span></h3>",
   "solution": "<h3><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mstyle></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1.1</mn><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>0.9</mn><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mstyle></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mrow><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0.99</mn><mo>&#x021D2;</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>99</mn><mrow><mtext>&#x000A0;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow></mrow></mstyle></math></h3>",
