   "question": "<h3>In a setup of displacement method experiment, distance between the screen and a light source is 150 cm and the lens used has a small aperture. By moving the lens between the source and the screen, sharp images are obtained on the screen for two different positions of the lens. The focal length of the lens is 24 cm . Find the ratio of the sizes of these two images formed on the screen.</h3>",
   "solution": "<h3><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi> f </mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi> D </mi><mrow><mn> 2 </mn></mrow></msup><mo>&minus;</mo><msup><mi> x </mi><mrow><mn> 2 </mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn> 4 </mn><mi> D </mi></mrow></mfrac><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math> <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msup><mi> x </mi><mrow><mn> 2 </mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi> D </mi><mrow><mn> 2 </mn></mrow></msup><mo>&minus;</mo><mn> 4 </mn><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> D </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> F </mi></mrow></mrow></math> <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi> x </mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi> D </mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi> D </mi><mo>&minus;</mo><mn> 4 </mn><mi> f </mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math> <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi> x </mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn> 150 </mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn> 150 </mn><mo>&minus;</mo><mn> 96 </mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math> <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi> x </mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn> 150 </mn><mi>&times;</mi><mn> 54 </mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></math> <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi> x </mi><mo>=</mo><mn> 90 </mn><mrow><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> c </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> m </mi></mrow></mrow></math> The ratio of the sizes of two images formed on the screen, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi> &beta; </mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi> D </mi><mo>+</mo><mi> x </mi></mrow><mrow><mi> D </mi><mo>&minus;</mo><mi> x </mi></mrow></mfrac><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn> 2 </mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math> <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi> &beta; </mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn> 150 </mn><mo>+</mo><mn> 90 </mn></mrow><mrow><mn> 150 </mn><mo>&minus;</mo><mn> 90 </mn></mrow></mfrac><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn> 2 </mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math> <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi> &beta; </mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn> 240 </mn></mrow><mrow><mn> 60 </mn></mrow></mfrac><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn> 2 </mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn> 4 </mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow><mn> 2 </mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn> 16 </mn></mrow></math></h3>",
