   "question": "<h3>(JEE Main 2021) If the kinetic energy of a body becomes four times of its initial value, then new momentum will<br />(A) Become twice its initial value<br />(B) Become three times, its initial value<br />(C) Become four times, its initial value<br />(D) Remains constant</h3>\n",
   "solution": "<h3><math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" ><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mstyle></math><br/><br/>When KE become four times then momentum (p) become two times.</h3>",
   "answer": "A",
