  "updatedAt": "2025-11-06T08:43:08.711Z",
  "scq": {
   "question": "<h3><span style=\"color:#000000\">Who provided the evidance for the producton of glucose when plant grows?</h3><h3>(A)<span style=\"color:#000000\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Julius von Sachs<br />(B)<span style=\"color:#000000\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Stephen Hales<br />(C)<span style=\"color:#000000\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\">Lavoisier<br />(D)</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Von Helmont</span></span></span></h3>",
   "solution": "<h3><span style=\"color:#000000\">Julius von Sachs provided evidence for the production of glucose when plants grow. Glucose is usually stored as starch. His later studies showed that the green substance in plants (chlorophyll as we know it now) is located in special bodies (later called chloroplast) within plant cells.<br />\r\n<span style=\"color:#000000\">He found that the green parts in plants are where glucose is made, and that the glucose is usually stored as starch</span></span></h3>",
   "answer": "A",
   "quesImages": [],
   "solutionImages": []
